Heated: Artefacts from the Near Future transforms architectural renders and product designs into speculative visions of climate futures. Upload a design render, choose a climate scenario — heatwave (44°C), flood (80mm/6h), windstorm (120km/h), or an AI-projected near future based on IPCC regional data — and the tool generates an AI-transformed speculative image of the design under those conditions, plus a short design-fiction narrative dispatched from that future.

Built with Gemini 2.5 Flash Image for the transformations, a Node/Express backend, Turso for shareable generations, and Vercel Blob for storage.

Check the project output [here](https://climate-render.heated.studio/).
